   "text": {
    "L1": "An expression joins numbers with operations and stands for a value.",
    "L2": "A common myth says you must fully calculate an expression before comparing it. Not true.",
    "L3": "A situation helps us write an expression: 3 samosas at 15 rupees and 2 chai at 10 rupees gives 3 × 15 + 2 × 10.",
    "L4": "We can compare by reasoning about parts, without full calculation.",
    "L5": "In 247 + 389 and 250 + 386, one part gains 3 and the other loses 3.",
    "L6": "The totals match, so 247 + 389 equals 250 + 386.",
    "L7": "For words, start with the number being changed: 12 less than 40 is 40 − 12.",
    "L8": "Now compare the two expressions and choose the relationship you can justify."
   },
